{"title":"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Similar_to_Solution_3)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Similar to Solution 3)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ordered_pair\" title=\"Ordered pair\">ordered pairs</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a> is it true that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9cec3ee548b5d66570b5e54a4a291628ea54702.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; y &lt; 10^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> and that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_mean\" title=\"Arithmetic mean\">arithmetic mean</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_mean\" title=\"Geometric mean\">geometric mean</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d6bef3bd348f48b01f9a0541d6eca279bf9549.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\frac{x+y}{2} &amp;=&amp; \\sqrt{xy} + 2\\\\ x+y-4 &amp;=&amp; 2\\sqrt{xy}\\\\ y - 2\\sqrt{xy} + x &amp;=&amp; 4\\\\ \\sqrt{y} - \\sqrt{x} &amp;=&amp; \\pm 2\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"221\" height=\"113\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d54b3e39757a5100c5b839497b8350d59f8c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, we only consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe54585e0c171194b0e07cc59767d097999658cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>For simplicity, we can count how many valid pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/99372baf723ef10f945f01f286efb8ba9f1ca7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{x},\\sqrt{y})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> that satisfy our equation.\n</p><p>The maximum that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce55298e9e1c0d0dacbc6d61c958f084007aba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> can be is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1dd5964522e5ada21d2d748a7d8af708976a224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{10^6} - 1 = 999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce55298e9e1c0d0dacbc6d61c958f084007aba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> must be an integer (this is because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df4743dc616bbf85872c574921bf518f9f708c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{y} - \\sqrt{x} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />, an integer). Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce277dea574f8395e0f572a548c8b841f9c1e4f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x} = 997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, and we continue this downward until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a74b510f95561d8539310ecfc1a0ffffcd849ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{y} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"60\" height=\"21\" />, in which case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/5/075c69e3faa98fc1d644406b0d3523ae49002ac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />. The number of pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/99372baf723ef10f945f01f286efb8ba9f1ca7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{x},\\sqrt{y})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c484f783ae105f16535383fe571942a1db8f3c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9698c992334be77221be8c8c819909eca34fde9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d03c3c5b9abf1bdb0c9df06fe5fb11ae13d0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a57653c68e8e9e118bd2dd240943a061307f6db2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2} = \\sqrt{{a^2}{b^2}} +2\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c1c235f2efb916b3bd876e38bdbf938f8268f06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 + b^2 = 2ab + 4\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cd2ff425cf7f68ea8f64a6b9b969eea0b51c279.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b)^2 = 4\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b1cfb63cbb6efc6b525ccded58662d33104238.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b) = \\pm 2\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This makes counting a lot easier since now we just have to find all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> that differ by 2.\n</p><p><br />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42b89f0587d464a974edf4e7dccd8e71b5b978ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{10^6} = 10^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"21\" />, then we can use all positive integers less than 1000 for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWe know that because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94c45489bc9bbeae5ab98827205179e938f7c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWe can count even and odd pairs separately to make things easier*:\n</p><p><br />\nOdd: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1e974b1489defd6aaccbe1bcdc000a3dcafdcc6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1,3) , (3,5) , (5,7)  .  .  .  (997,999)\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nEven: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c832904f7a3a0d52fb5687d970fd66de7f3b865.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2,4) , (4,6) , (6,8)  .  .  .  (996,998)\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThis makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/6500248a8e3334fcfb20b237b0e343980327ad17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$499$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> odd pairs and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dc24b1aaec28fb0b55f9aad56bbf1de8d80aa7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$498$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> even pairs, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c484f783ae105f16535383fe571942a1db8f3c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> pairs.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />Note: We are counting the pairs for the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, which, when squared, translate to the pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> we are trying to find.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since the arithmetic mean is 2 more than the geometric mean, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/f/9efb6ca4b9ea6c6cded2eea2656433c2301fd0bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+y}{2} = 2 + \\sqrt{xy}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"137\" height=\"35\" />. We can multiply by 2 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709243f03e07380063e581c562adf700c5e0b8ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 4 + 2\\sqrt{xy}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />. Subtracting 4 and squaring gives \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526c75ee450d39c7b6cdc5fce3e53dbb0d920628.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[((x+y)-4)^2 = 4xy\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76dc0463e6e20ff3d6aedc12e85566336ef5402e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[((x^2 + 2xy + y^2) + 16 - 2(4)(x+y)) = 4xy\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34b6c39b26523ecdc8c847d9c895c5605f533660.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - 2xy + y^2 + 16 - 8x - 8y = 0\\]\" width=\"263\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/714c0306ffd7bcde8c99003c5e8476a2651e7f5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((x-y)-4)^2 = x^2 - 2xy + y^2 + 16 - 8x +8y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"364\" height=\"19\" />, so the problem asks for solutions of \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed76d6f12a963181e041d053b4785881fa578be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-y-4)^2 = 16y\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"19\" />\nSince the left hand side is a perfect square, and 16 is a perfect square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must also be a perfect square. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae217cf2890eb2e7e547a7b093891dbab7977ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; y &lt; (1000)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c716d1dc907ae6b51cb0f545664c89d58b6b67d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac5c2b27b6d40e5480c0e41e0c71b28f0ef6bc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999^2$\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />, giving at most 999 options for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>However if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bd4caaa9b44d9dabfb9b28d48b2cf990325614e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56e39d679d3d5b1d09291277459cc15080e1838.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-5)^2 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" />, which has solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a7a2005b67ab81ee5ff231b2f370f1d71ebe1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 9$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Both of those solutions are not less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be equal to 1. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd1f539342c04aae7d184d7b6eb4de8bbef3c718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/4107ed5bc9abc69ccddee936f40291ce5e730884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 8)^2 = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" />, which has 2 solutions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2cae13a8f6458d5d8c61ba965d0abb4b08da072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. 16 is not less than 4, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be 0, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be 4. However, for all other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, you get exactly 1 solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and that gives a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c78880123dc910dd39198563ad2123a53de92674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999 - 2 = \\boxed{997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" /> pairs.\n</p><p>- asbodke\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Similar_to_Solution_3.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Similar_to_Solution_3)\">Solution 4 (Similar to Solution 3)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Similar to Solution 3)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Rearranging our conditions to \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df7f31a7864d558ef4fc74494d96122d2fdf708a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2-2xy+y^2+16-8x-8y=0 \\implies\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26029b6d5b9da7a9ff3ef8c2e38d5332a60b8f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(y-x)^2=8(x+y-2).\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9b5b85dbea808d7c4f08cb14e8d782cb4182a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4|y-x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/f/a3fb38c186654622ee3963c3f29b9ce87ac211db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 4k+x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> Plugging this back into our expression, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/435b01901c0394c6c0dfe0ae56b4538eb0e8380c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(k-1)^2=x.\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>There, a unique value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> is formed for every value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. However, we must have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffb63c126c6361902cd21ec22b92503cb3fcd286.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y&lt;10^6 \\implies (k+1)^2&lt; 10^6-1\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>and \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/587f473446e9a5366892e7509fbbf0b4e5abba1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=(k-1)^2+1&gt;0.\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c484f783ae105f16535383fe571942a1db8f3c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/101897204ba9a49f7e0e2646a7b9fb7f8bbb0a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"49\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Solution by Williamgolly\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First we see that our condition is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/f/9efb6ca4b9ea6c6cded2eea2656433c2301fd0bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+y}{2} = 2 + \\sqrt{xy}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"137\" height=\"35\" />. Then we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c113f4b49386305e8ae60927574dc75bca9f467a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y = 4 + 2\\sqrt{xy}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" />. From trying a simple example to figure out conditions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />, we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643e1765342cf3807fd7d130ee679b71ecd4789b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> so we can isolate for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. From doing the example we can note that we can square both sides and subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/8334912c098b3674703b7b158f8155b51027d976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/679ab93bf0bde554b3c900ca4647b1456aefc099.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-y)^2 = 16 + 16\\sqrt{xy} \\implies x-y = -2( \\sqrt{1+\\sqrt{xy}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"421\" height=\"34\" /> (note it is negative because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d54b3e39757a5100c5b839497b8350d59f8c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. Clearly the square root must be an integer, so now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f8129d0be54776e53d59c3ffb023c40c49db6c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{xy} = a^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"110\" height=\"22\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/ddee8c760b9b4977efa4d945443d4382be3b618e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y = -2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c7ef6bf6057249c6d7892fe4c19039185000c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2 + \\sqrt{xy} - a = 2 + a^2 - 1 -2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"280\" height=\"22\" />. We can then find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and use the quadratic formula on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> to ensure they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f040b184e0e6eaa9464f09c389a6f60fcf1f27c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b63ff2f97e73c2af7c6fcc828c7b5c9826ebc3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;10^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. Thus we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> can go up to 999 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can go down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/90782e3f18f6a430876413c43e3d163e0e8ae3f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$997$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I\" title=\"2000 AIME I\">2000 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183826\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 621/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18756/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.368      1 -total\n 59.31%    7.336      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.91%    4.812      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3047:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183826 and revision id 239672. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}